{"title":"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is inside square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> so that each side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> can be extended to pass through a vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6d1b584a42c88275d2ae86a59079aad25c034f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7edf3afba191eb9958ab78c986da35e33e1681b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. What is the area of the inner square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/63933d5d224cb8b1a275205d6c3c0baab193dd47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); pair D=(0,0), C=(1,0), B=(1,1), A=(0,1); pair F=intersectionpoints(Circle(D,2/sqrt(5)),Circle(A,1))[0]; pair G=foot(A,D,F), H=foot(B,A,G), E=foot(C,B,H); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(D--F); draw(C--E); draw(B--H); draw(A--G); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,NNW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,ENE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,SSE); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,WSW); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"225\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810dfcecc71022276e274ca22ebc746a5c2e7fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\mathrm {A}) \\ 25 \\qquad (\\mathrm {B}) \\ 32 \\qquad (\\mathrm {C})\\ 36 \\qquad (\\mathrm {D}) \\ 40 \\qquad (\\mathrm {E})\\ 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2005_12A_AMC-7b.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/f8/2005_12A_AMC-7b.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"366\" height=\"362\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Arguable the hardest part of this question is to visualize the diagram. Since each side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> can be extended to pass through a vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> must be tilted in such a fashion. Let a side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2005_12A_AMC-7.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/ec/2005_12A_AMC-7.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"419\" height=\"402\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Notice the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a> (in blue) with legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b2ef0d728e55041038290fd992ffb8da668b2ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hypotenuse\" title=\"Hypotenuse\">hypotenuse</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6d1b584a42c88275d2ae86a59079aad25c034f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11e20007dad331a20146f0f381d71966cfc600d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2 + (x+1)^2 = (\\sqrt{50})^2 \\Longrightarrow (x+1)^2 = 49 \\Longrightarrow x = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"409\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d30f9bca378f43e18618306b3247b27128bf96f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[EFGH] = x^2 = 36\\ \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A\">2005 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=